<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Intel trading lower.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Intel trading lower.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intel Corp and Cisco Systems Inc were down in after-hours trading Friday, after a day in which technology stocks led the Nasdaq Composite index to a 13.09 point decline.</p>
<p>Intel was trading at 145-5/8, after closing at 146-3/8, traders said. It fell 3-1/2 points during regular trading.</p>
<p>Cisco was trading at 58 after the bell. It had closed at 58-3/8, down 4-5/8 for the day.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said session one volume was 158,900, compared to Thursday's volume of 96,200. Session two volume was 10,578,553, compared with 1,856,000 on Thursday.</p>
